wiringPi Debian Package Split
=============================

This package has been split into three separate binary packages:

  libwiringpi3  - Runtime library only (GPIO functions)
  libwiringpi-dev - Development files (headers, symlinks)
  wiringpi      - gpio command line utility

Why the split?
  - The library soname changed from libwiringPi.so.2 to libwiringPi.so.3
    in WiringPi 3.x, requiring a new package name to avoid conflicts.
  - Separating the dev files allows independent installation.
  - The wiringpi binary depends only on the runtime library.

Installation
------------

  sudo apt install libwiringpi3 wiringpi   # runtime + utility
  sudo apt install libwiringpi-dev         # headers & symlinks

Usage
-----

  gpio -export all out
  gpio -mode 0 out
  gpio -write 0 1

For full documentation, see:
  /usr/share/doc/wiringpi/
  /usr/share/doc/libwiringpi3/

Notes
-----

- The utility requires wiringPi board setup (run gpio readall first time).
- Header files are in /usr/include/ and symlinked via libwiringpi-dev.
- ABI compatibility: libwiringPi.so.3 is the soname; links against
  -lwiringPi expect this library.

See also:
  /usr/share/doc/wiringpi/changelog.Debian.gz
  /usr/share/doc/libwiringpi3/copyright
